            <ArticleTitle>Concurrence of multiples factors in the occurrence of ventricular arrhythmia in patient treated with aripiprazole.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>346-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="INTRODUCTION" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">The Importance of the cardiovascular effects, fundamentally the ventricular arrhythmias, produced by the antipsychotic ones, is discussed.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CLINICAL CASE" NlmCategory="METHODS">28 year old patient with morbid obesity, operated by bariatric surgery, with good result, suffers a ventricular no supported polymorphic tachycardia while he was heightening treatment with aripiprazole and fluoxetine.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">To value the influence of diverse factors for the production of ventricular arrhythmias emphasizing fundamentally the interactions of aripiprazole and the loss of weight.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
